    "narrative": "The anchor of our lineup today is **James Wood**, who commands an elite score of 72.75. Facing Alcantara, he benefits from a highly favorable 4.41 xERA matchup and a blistering 88% stolen base probability against the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, making him our primary engine for both counting stats and our critical scarce category. **Corbin Carroll** also clears the \"Strong\" threshold at 60.41; despite a tougher matchup against Emmet Sheehan, **Corbin Carroll**\u2019s elite .372 xwOBA and aggressive batting position in the two-hole ensure he remains a must-start as we hunt for SB upside. **Brice Turang** earns a strong 55.22, buoyed by a prime #3 order slot that maximizes his exposure in a high-leverage context against Roupp.\n\nThe primary lineup construction challenge today involves balancing mid-tier options against our strict 40.0 efficiency floor. **Josh Naylor** (54.73) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (54.25) anchor the corners effectively, with **Vinnie Pasquantino** specifically benefiting from a +14% dynamic platoon boost. Our closest call on the bench was **Cole Young**, whose 37.07 score fell just shy of the threshold. While **Cole Young** possesses the profile to potentially jump into the lineup, the combination of a park factor drag and a tough matchup against Austin Warren kept him on the bench to preserve our game caps. **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland** remain active despite the \"Lineup Pending\" tag, though their sub-50 scores against Eduardo Rodriguez require monitoring; if either is dropped lower in the order than our projections suggest, their value will plummet further. We are monitoring **Kyle Karros** (41.86) closely as well; while he cleared our floor, his score is suppressed by facing an elite defensive catcher and a tough matchup, making him the most precarious starter in today\u2019s set.",
